# Kandelo patch rationale (S21)
#
# Node diagnostics need real compilation identity and source after scripts
# or contexts disappear. Capture generic facts while the script is live and
# retain one opaque native metadata reference per saved frame. The bridge
# owns the shared source registry and release policy; a filename lookup would
# confuse distinct compilations, and the OS cannot capture engine provenance.
# The hook contains no untraced JS edges and may not run JavaScript.
#
# Source-only cleanup; not rebuilt or behavior-qualified. Retention remains
# subject to README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

